  ('Valparaíso', 'Chile', -33.0472, -71.6127, 1888, '/rounds/Valparaiso_1888.png', 'Valparaíso in 1888 is represented as a steep Pacific port with hills, maritime commerce, and late-19th-century urban texture.', ARRAY['Steep hills descending to a harbor and dense hillside housing', 'Pacific port infrastructure with ships, warehouses, docks, or stairways', 'South American coastal terrain rather than inland plains']::text[], ARRAY['Late-19th-century clothing, sailing or steam vessels, and horse-era streets', 'Pre-automobile urban life before modern port equipment', 'Avoid container cranes, modern roads, and contemporary hillside towers']::text[], 'Do not show the name of the location anywhere in the image. Do not include visible text, captions, labels, map names, titles, or signage that explicitly reveals the city, country, or exact place. Avoid readable signage unless it is generic and non-revealing. The image must contain clues, but must not directly state the answer.', 'approved', 'manual', 4, true),
