  ('Lima', 'Peru', -12.0464, -77.0428, 1920, '/rounds/Lima_1920.png', 'Lima in 1920 is represented as a Pacific coastal capital with colonial balconies, arid light, plazas, and early-20th-century urban life.', ARRAY['Dry coastal atmosphere, colonial wooden balconies, plazas, and low-rise civic architecture', 'Pacific South American capital setting without rainforest or high mountain streets', 'Churches, arcades, tramlines, or historic center streets']::text[], ARRAY['Early-20th-century clothing, trams, horse carts, and few early cars', 'Republican-era city life rather than colonial or late-modern scenes', 'Avoid concrete expressways, contemporary buses, and glass high-rises']::text[], 'Do not show the name of the location anywhere in the image. Do not include visible text, captions, labels, map names, titles, or signage that explicitly reveals the city, country, or exact place. Avoid readable signage unless it is generic and non-revealing. The image must contain clues, but must not directly state the answer.', 'approved', 'manual', 3, true),
